  "camera_differentiation": {
    "_why": "Camera placement could NOT be verified in-process: `getall PlayerController Location` prints nothing because Location is not a UPROPERTY on the controller. Cross-station variation is the only available check -- if BugItGo moved nothing, all four stations would be the SAME view and their GPU cost would match.",
    "gpu_p90_by_zone": {
      "plaza": 8.334,
      "main_street": 5.945,
      "treeline": 5.578,
      "vista": 6.988
    },
    "gpu_p90_relative_spread": 0.4941,
    "verdict": "PASS: GPU p90 varies 49% across the four stations (5.58 to 8.33 ms), which one fixed view cannot produce. The camera moved.",
    "game_p90_relative_spread": 0.0519,
    "_note_on_game_flatness": "The GAME thread is nearly flat across stations in standalone too (3.85-4.05 ms). That is NOT the failure signature: the GPU varies, so the view changed. It says the game thread is not driven by what is on screen at these stations -- in standalone it sits near 3.9 ms rather than the editor's ~14."
  },
