      }
    ],
    "_the_finding": "The editor's FrameTime p50 sits at 16.67 ms at every station -- a 60 Hz cap, not a measurement of cost. Its GameThreadTime tracks that cap (13.4-14.0) rather than the content, which is exactly what REGISTER recorded as 'pinned at 13.9-14.15 ms on all four zones regardless of content'. With the editor gone the game thread drops to ~3.9 ms while the GPU stays within a few percent of the editor's figure -- the GPU was measuring the scene all along; the game thread was measuring the harness.",
    "_CAVEAT_NOT_LIKE_FOR_LIKE": "The GPU columns are NOT strictly comparable. The editor baseline records viewport_size = None for every zone -- it never captured the resolution it ran at, so there is no way to confirm it rendered at 3840x2160. The standalone side reads 4K back from the CsvProfiler metadata. A GPU figure is resolution-bound, so treat the GPU rows as INDICATIVE. The GAME THREAD comparison does not depend on resolution and is the load-bearing one.",
    "editor_viewport_size_recorded": {
      "plaza": null,
      "main_street": null,
      "treeline": null,
      "vista": null
    }
  },
  "_reproduction_attempt_2026_09_08": {
    "outcome": "FAILED TWICE, for an environmental reason, not a disagreement with the result.",
    "what_happened": "Both attempts returned 'no CSV appeared within the window' at every station. The log shows the level never finished loading: shader jobs were still dispatching (8,263 then 7,801) when the dwell expired, so CsvProfile never started.",
    "cause": "I EMPTIED C:/UnrealDDC EARLIER THIS SESSION to reclaim 92 GB during a disk crisis. The original measurement ran against a WARM cache and settled in 60 s; the reproduction paid the full shader-compile cost from an empty one. Observed directly: the DDC was refilling through the attempt, 0 -> 11.31 GB.",
    "settle_tried": [
      105,
      420
    ],
    "not_a_reason_to_doubt_the_result": "The failure is in the instrument's SETUP TIME, not in what it measured. No number changed; no station produced a different figure. The original four-station measurement stands as recorded above.",
    "cost_recorded": "A disk cleanup at 19:00 caused a failed measurement at 22:20. Freeing a derived-data cache is reversible in principle and expensive in practice -- the engine rebuilds it, but only by spending the time again, and any measurement in between pays for it.",
    "to_reproduce": "scripts/perf_standalone.py --only plaza --settle 900, once the DDC has refilled from ordinary use. The tool now takes --settle for exactly this."
  }
